# Gentleman + LIDR Ecosystem Bridge

Registry (SSOT): [`docs/governance/GENTLEMAN_ECOSYSTEM_REGISTRY.json`](../../docs/governance/GENTLEMAN_ECOSYSTEM_REGISTRY.json)
Decision: [`ADR-0019`](../../docs/architecture/adrs/ADR-0019-gentleman-ecosystem-integration-registry.md) amends [`ADR-0010`](../../docs/architecture/adrs/ADR-0010-lidr-specboot-gentleman-discipline-bridge.md)
Gate: `scripts/lib/gentleman-ecosystem-lock.js` (fail-closed in `npm run verify:strict`)

EOS is an independent project. This bridge implies **no endorsement, sponsorship, or official affiliation** with Gentleman Programming or LIDR Academy. Gentle AI and Engram are trademarks of Alan Buscaglia; upstream MIT licensing covers code only. **No upstream file body is vendored into this repository** — concepts are mapped, bodies stay upstream.

## 1. Vocabulary (do not drift)

| Acronym | Canonical expansion | Meaning in EOS |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **ODD** | Organic Driven Development | Default everyday workflow: smallest honest route |
| **SDD** | Spec-Driven Development | OpenSpec ceremony, entered on purpose (ADR-0010 §2) |
| **RDD** | Receipt-Driven Development | Truth from frozen artifacts, never from narration (`CONSTITUTION.md` Article I §2) |
| **4R** | Risk, Resilience, Readability, Reliability | The four review lenses, applied only at high depth |

`RDD` is **Receipt**-Driven Development. The earlier reading in ADR-0010 §4 is superseded by ADR-0019; the ADR body stays byte-stable as an accepted record.

## 2. ODD routing — the smallest honest route

Run ODD on every request. Size alone never escalates ceremony; ambiguity and blast radius do.

1. **Stay read-only until a change is authorised.** Investigation, explanation, and audit never edit files.
2. **Explore before editing**, so nothing is implemented on top of a false assumption.
3. **Route by understanding, not by line count.** One to three well-understood files: work directly. Four or more, or unfamiliar ground: send one focused explorer first.
4. **Substantial authorised work gets one recoverable document.** In EOS that document is the OpenSpec change directory under `openspec/changes/<change-id>/`, not an ad-hoc scratch file.
5. **Implement task by task**, keeping progress current so a cold session can resume without rebuilding the plan.
6. **Close with observed evidence** — recorded command output, never a claim of success.

SDD is a branch inside ODD that you enter deliberately (explicit request, accepted proposal, new contract or subsystem, external write). It is never the default for a one-line fix. `NO_BUILD` stays a valid outcome.

## 3. RDD — depth comes from the frozen candidate

Freeze what is under review **before** reading it, so the evidence belongs to the exact revision you are about to rely on and not to whatever the worktree looked like a moment later. In EOS the frozen candidate is a committed revision plus `git diff` output and the sealed receipt under `docs/evidence/`.

| Depth | Trigger | Required review work |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Passive | Docs, comments, formatting | Structural readback; zero lenses |
| Medium | Local behaviour change inside one bounded area | One focused lens, chosen from the 4R by the dominant risk |
| High | New contract, governance surface, security path, external write | All four lenses: Risk, Resilience, Readability, Reliability |

At most **one bounded correction** per review transaction; a second round means the change was not ready and goes back to ODD. Review outcome is **INFORMATIONAL**: it never authorises merge, release, or an external write. Those stay human-owned under `CONSTITUTION.md` Article II–III.

## 4. Engram memory — context, never evidence

Protocol and tool surface live in [`engram.mdc`](./engram.mdc). Two hard rules:

- Memory is **working context**. A sealed receipt under `docs/evidence/` is the only evidence of record (`ADR-0016`).
- Never write a secret, token, or credential into memory (Law VI). Store opaque handles and digests only.

## 5. Refused and watched imports

| Upstream | Stance | Why |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `gentle-ai` binary as an in-repo installer | REFUSE | No foreign installer in an L0 repository; operators may run it on their own machine |
| `gga` pre-commit hook installation | ADAPT, not installed | `AGENTS.md` stays the reviewable standard; a hook that calls an external provider in the commit path is an unreviewed network dependency |
| `agent-teams-lite` | REFUSE | Upstream archived and deprecated; must not be cited as a live design source |
| `gentleman-architecture-agents` (Scope Rule) | REFUSE | No upstream license declared, and Scope Rule is frontend placement — NON-core here (ADR-0010 §4.3) |
| `Gentleman.Dots` | REFUSE | Workstation configuration is out of scope for a control plane |
| `gentle-shell`, `manual-SDD` | WATCH | Pi runtime / unlicensed reference; revisit only through a new decision record |

Before adding, citing, or vendoring any upstream component, update the registry first. The lock fails closed on a surface that does not exist, on a stance attached to an archived upstream, and on superseded vocabulary anywhere in the governed tree.
